Usage: getconf [OPTION]... [VARIABLE_NAME]...
getconf [OPTION]... PATH_VAR PATH

Display configuration variable values.

If no VARIABLE_NAME is specified, display system-dependent limit values.
On Windows, this provides limited system configuration information.

Options:
  -a, --all  display all configuration variables
  -v SPEC    give values for compilation environment SPEC

OPTIONS:
  -a, --all      display all configuration variables
  -v ARG         give values for compilation environment SPEC
                 get system configuration values
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
